+# 🧩 GeometryProcessing
+
+**TL;DR**: This is a from-scratch, Parasolid-style B-rep modeller.
+- Step 1 covers precision, topology, Euler edits and analytic geometry.
+- Step 2 covers Bézier-clipping root solving, curve–surface intersection and hybrid surface–surface intersection.
+- Step 3 adds generalized-winding-number containment and General Fuse Booleans (OCCT-style PaveFiller + Builder, all four operations from one fuse).
+- Step 4 adds watertight shared-edge tessellation: one sampling per edge, used by every face that touches it, and a constrained Delaunay triangulation per face in its parameter chart.
+- Step 5 adds rolling-ball fillets and chamfers. The spine is the intersection of the two offset surfaces (Choi–Ju). Exact Cylinder, Torus, Cone, Plane and corner Sphere carriers are trimmed at caps, mitres and ball corners. The body is rebuilt by assembly with face history, and every refusal is atomic.
+- Step 6 adds the generic face change (research § K) and offsets (§ J). Each selected face gets a new carrier: offset, translated, scaled, rotated, drafted or replaced by a rim. Its edges and vertices are re-solved by intersecting the neighbouring carriers, and the body is rebuilt by assembly. Push, tweak, offset, scale, rotate, draft, extend, trim, offset-body, hollow, extrude, delete, heal and thicken are thin wrappers over that one algorithm. An edge/face clash probe refuses self-intersecting results.
+- Step 7 adds the sketch solver (research § M), persistent names (§ L) and the feature tree. The solver runs Gauss–Newton and Levenberg–Marquardt on the full system, and a rank-revealing QR of J gives DOF, redundant constraints and conflict groups. Every face, edge and vertex gets a history name such as `Extrude#2.Side(Line1)`. A tree regenerates by replay; each reference resolves exact → same source → geometric rebind, and anything ambiguous is refused, never guessed. A bevel now follows its sketch, which closes G1.
+- Step 8 closes kernel gaps G2–G5, and the old FeatureSuitability corpus replays with **0 refusals** (the old kernel refused 19 of 176 rows). G2: a pipe on an arc is the section circle revolved about the arc axis (exact partial torus). G3: marched sections become exact `IntersectionCurve` carriers (a Hermite guide plus Newton onto both surfaces), so General Fuse accepts CrossUnequal. G4: equal crossing cylinders (Steinmetz) are solved analytically as half-ellipses split at the 2 singular points, which become fuse vertices. G5: after assembly, `RemoveRedundantTopology` merges faces across edges between pieces of one oriented carrier and joins edges across degree-two vertices, giving maximal faces (BoxUnion: 14 → 6 faces). New verbs: `PipeAlongPath`, `LoftCircles`, `SweepProfileAlongLine`, partial revolve, `TransformBody` / `MirrorBody` / `ArrayBody` / `TransformBodyAcross`.
+
+A C++ library is inspected through a Python host and a single-page HTML viewer that rebuilds whenever a source file changes.
+
+## Status: steps 1–8 of the build order
+
+| Area | Content | Gate |
+|---|---|---|
+| A. Precision | Session/angular precision, local (tolerant) precision per edge and vertex, Shewchuk adaptive `Orient2D` / `Orient3D` | 🟢 PredicateValidation: 0 wrong out of 800 000 |
+| B. Topology | Body → Region → SolidShell → Face → Loop → Fin → Edge → Vertex, generation-checked tokens | 🟢 T1–T5 audit after every edit |
+| C. Euler edits | MVFS/KVFS, MEV/KEV, MEF/KEF, MEKR/KEMR, KFMRH/MFKRH, ReverseShellOrientation, TransferShell, DetachShell | 🟢 14 specimens torn down to an empty partition |
+| D. Geometry | Line, circle, ellipse (`ConicForm`), intersection curve (exact, guide + Newton), contact rail (foot of a spine on a support); plane, cylinder, cone, sphere, torus, offset surface, rolling-ball pipe P(𝑢, 𝑣) = C(𝑢) + r(cos 𝑣 E₁ + sin 𝑣 E₂) on any spine (procedural, exact on its definition); SP-curves (line, ellipse) | 🟢 Volume by quadrature, relative error ≤ 1.62e-15 (TopologyValidation A, 14 specimens) |
+| E. Root solving + CSI | Bernstein algebra, Bézier clipping (Sederberg–Nishita), exact rational Bézier arcs composed into implicit surfaces (degree ≤ 8), roots of F and F′, Newton polish on the exact distance, tangent and coincident detection | 🟢 IntersectionValidation E1/E2: 60 000 polynomials, all within the condition bound; 2 000 random curve–surface pairs, 0 of 3 183 sign changes missed |
+| F. Hybrid SSI | Analytic dispatch (plane–plane, coaxial meridians, parallel sections, plane through an axis, equal crossing cylinders as half-ellipses), then lattice + boundary seeds, normal-cone loop detection, 3D-corrector marching, singular-point splitting | 🟢 F1: 3 500 random analytic cases ≤ 5.4e-15. F2: marching on the exact curves (≤ 7.6e-15). F3: 22 gallery runs + 300 random oblique pairs sound, and the negative control is caught |
+| G. General Fuse Booleans | PaveFiller: EE, EF, FF interferences (exact SSI; marched sections become exact intersection-curve carriers, G3; singular points become fuse vertices, G4), paves, pave blocks, common blocks, section splitting, imprint. Builder: face splitting by smallest-turn cycle tracing in the chart, outer/hole assignment, fragment classification (GWN, plus normals for on-boundary fragments). Selection and assembly for ∪ ∩ − with history (Modified / Generated), then maximal faces and edges (`RemoveRedundantTopology`, G5) | 🟢 BooleanValidation: 23 closed-form scenes × 4 operations + 160 random pairs; audit sound, ΔV ≤ 6.5e-15, identities ≤ 5.3e-14, 0 of 26 400 oracle points wrong; an open argument is refused |
+| H. Containment | Projected SP-curves (`ParameterProjection`), face domains in the chart, 2D parameter winding, 3D generalized winding number Σ Ω_F / 4π by Green in the chart (adaptive Gauss–Kronrod). Proximity first, then the nearest-normal shortcut, then winding | 🟢 ContainmentValidation H1–H6: 12 000 random points, normal offsets down to 1e-7, on-boundary points, ray-cast parity, open-box Van Oosterom–Strackee, 2D holes; 0 wrong, integer residual ≤ 3.2e-13 |
+| N. Shared-edge CDT tessellation | Exact `InCircle`; Bowyer–Watson CDT with exact cavity repair, Sloan constraint recovery, parity classification (`ChartTriangulation`). Per edge: adaptive τ bisection to sag ε, a √(8ε/κ) chord bound and chart fidelity on every fin. Per face: linear chart scaled by \|S_u\|, \|S_v\|; Ruppert-style refinement on 3D sag (distance to the surface) and side length, with a quality floor; pole and apex stars rebuilt from the chart boundary of the star; 3D side flips of folded slivers; split of interior sides another face already used | 🟢 TessellationValidation: 342 bodies (14 specimens, 23 scenes × 4 less 4 empty results, 240 random Boolean results), 725 172 triangles. 0 unpaired sides, χ equal, peak ≤ ε, 0 inverted / zero-area / folded, \|ΔV\| ≤ 0.48 ε·A, 0 missing edge sides. Convergence slopes ≈ 1, deterministic digests, scale-free 10⁻³…10³, 201 CDT regressions |
+| J + K. Face change and offsets | `PlanFaceChange`: new carrier per selected face (offset, similarity motion, draft hinge at the neutral plane: plane → plane, cylinder → cone), every edge re-solved as kept / intersected / seam / laminar (exact plane–plane, plane–cylinder circle or ellipse, coaxial and cone sections), every vertex re-solved from three carriers, intervals re-derived, then `AssembleBody`. `ApplyFaceOperation`: 14 verbs over it. Topology rebuilds (`ExtrudePlanarFaces` side ring, `DeleteBodyFaces` hole heal or open sheet, `HealBody` carrier merge plus fin splicing, `ThickenSheet` inner skin plus rim faces). `HollowBody` = cavity by face change, then General Fuse difference. `DetectSelfClash`: every edge against every non-incident face | 🟢 FaceOperationValidation E1–E9: corpus section E 36/36 with **0 refusals on HoleSlab / Can (old FaceEditSolver: 17)**, chains 6/6, extras 12/12, refusals 8/8. V vs closed form ≤ 5.0e-15, edges on both carriers ≤ 2.6e-16·L, tessellation N gates (sheets by sheet rules), 0 of 2 210 winding probes wrong, chains ≡ reference ≤ 3.8e-16, deterministic, scale 10⁻³…10³ ≤ 1.2e-14 |
+| M. Sketch solver | `SolveSketch`: points and curves (line, circle, arc, construction flag) with 21 constraint kinds; residuals scaled to length; minimum-norm Gauss–Newton with an LM fallback; column-pivoted QR in constraint order for rank, DOF, the redundant set (the later member of a dependent set is blamed) and conflict groups (dependent rows whose residual stays); structural rank = the rank of the same system at a deterministically perturbed generic configuration; singular when structural rank > rank or conditioning < 10⁻³ × the generic configuration; fixed-point flags from the null space. `ExtractSketchProfile`: closed loops, area, centroid; open, branching or crossing loops are refused | 🟢 SketchValidation S1–S9: 18/18 sketches, DOF / redundant / conflicts equal to the hand count, positions vs closed form ≤ 1.1e-15·L, random starts 100 %, minimum-norm motion, fixed flags, scale 10⁻³…10³ ≤ 1.8e-16, singularity flagged exactly where expected, profile area ≤ 1.3e-15, deterministic; a 122-unknown chain at DOF 0 |
+| L. Persistent names + feature tree | `ExtrudeProfile`, `RevolveProfile` (`ProfileSweep`). `TopologicalNaming`: face names from operation history (`Extrude#2.Side(Line1)`, `Cap(End)`, `Blend#3.Strip(Edge(…))`, `Corner(Vertex(…))`, Boolean keeps source names, split pieces `/1`, `/2`); edge and vertex names from their faces (`Edge(A\|B)#k`); a signature (category, centroid, size) per name. `ResolveReference`: exact, then unique after stripping disambiguators, then geometric rebind (same category, size ratio ½…2, best clearly ahead), otherwise refused with the candidates. `RegenerateFeatureTree`: Sketch, Extrude, Revolve, Boolean, Blend and FaceOperation steps replayed from scratch; a refused step keeps the previous body and later steps still run. **Multi-body:** the replay keeps every body, keyed by the label of the step that created it (`RegenerationOutcome.Bodies`, `.Active`). Combination `Separate` (new body) starts one; `Step.Target` names the body a Boolean, blend or face edit acts on (empty = the active body); `Combine` merges `Tool` into `Target` (union / difference / intersection, tool consumed, sheets refused 🚧); the last body built or changed is active and `Outcome.Body` / `.Naming` | 🟢 FeatureValidation F1–F7 (single body, unchanged) · SolidArc W16 (multi-body, 10 checks): 7 trees, 33 regenerations, V vs closed form ≤ 2.1e-15, refused set = oracle and audit sound, 255 namings complete and unique, 1 164 survivors (74 renumbered by index, 18 renamed) all resolve to themselves, refused steps keep the previous body, expected methods (Exact 30 · Geometric 2 · Refused 3), deterministic |
+| I. Rolling-ball blends | `ResolveEdgeBlendSheet`: convexity from (n₀ × n₁)·(t·σ); fillet radius r or chamfer setback d (r = d·tan(θ/2)); spine = SSI of the two offset surfaces; carrier Cylinder / Torus (fillet) or Plane / Cone / Cylinder (chamfer). `BlendEdges`: vertex classes Cap (planar end face), Mitre (two blends, elliptical seam), BallCorner (three convex fillets, sphere), Continuation; contact rails trimmed against each other; rebuilt with `AssembleBody` (shared with General Fuse), then audit, then the genus is compared. The source body is never touched | 🟢 BlendValidation B1–B10: rolling-ball harness 15/15, BevelLab 6/6, 27 specimens. ΔV vs closed form ≤ 7.0e-16, G1 ≤ 3.6e-15 rad, rolling-ball law ≤ 1.6e-15 over 71 037 samples, tessellation N gates, 0 of 2 400 winding points wrong, 4 Booleans downstream ≤ 3.4e-16, 5 atomic refusals, deterministic, ΔV ∝ s³ to 7.7e-14 |
+| G2–G5. Gap closure + corpus replay | G2 `PipeAlongPath` (line → cylinder; arc → partial or full torus by revolving the section about the arc axis), `LoftCircles` (coaxial → frustum), `SweepProfileAlongLine`, partial `RevolveProfile`. G3 `IntersectionCurve`: C(τ) = the point of S₁ ∩ S₂ in the normal plane of a cubic Hermite guide, Newton per evaluation, split at knots for quadrature. G4 `SolveEqualCylinders` + `ClassifySpecialPoints` (Singular / Touch on the exact carrier). G5 `RemoveRedundantTopology` (KEF merge, slit removal, KVE join; `CountRedundantEdges` audits the same condition), on by default in `AssembleBoolean`. `BodyTransform`: similarity maps rebuild the body by assembly (translate, rotate, mirror, array, uniform scale; across partitions) | 🟢 CorpusValidation R1–R5: 79/79 rows (71 corpus rows of sections A–H plus 8 section-X scenes), **0 refused; 19 of 19 old refusals now exact**, V vs closed form ≤ 3.59e-14, audit sound with sources untouched, 0 redundant edges (ExtrudeFaces keeps its ring by definition), tessellation N gates. CrossOffset: the old kernel's 4.009803 was wrong (true 4.0099890528) |
+| O. NURBS carriers | `NurbsCurve` / `NurbsSurface` (rational, clamped, optional periodic seam): A2.1–A2.3 basis and derivatives (Piegl–Tiller), rational Leibniz derivatives to second order, lattice-seeded Newton inversion with box clamping, Boehm insertion and Bézier extraction, iso-curves, affine images on the poles. Exact conversions: line (degree 1, τ kept), circle and ellipse (rational quadratic per ≤ 90° with τ matched at the joints), plane, cylinder, cone, sphere, torus (rational revolution). Dispatch through evaluation, inversion, SSI (lattice seeds and marching on the exact distance), curve–surface (NURBS curves as Bézier pieces composed into implicit surfaces; NURBS surfaces by an exact signed-distance scan), General Fuse, containment, quadrature (𝑣-knot stops, domain base), tessellation curvature, face change and redundant-topology merge. `PromoteBodyToNurbs`; non-similar `TransformBody` (non-uniform scale, shear) promotes curved faces instead of refusing | 🟢 NurbsValidation N1–N7: conics and quadrics reproduced ≤ 8.5e-16 (normal ≤ 1.7e-14 rad), derivatives vs Richardson ≤ 4.1e-9, inversion ≤ 1.2e-13, iso / Bézier / reversal ≤ 6.7e-16, affine images ≤ 1.5e-15 with ellipsoid / elliptic bodies V = det·V* there and back, 8 promoted bodies (primitives, filleted block, bored disc) ≤ 9.6e-16 with 0 of 500 oracle points wrong, 5 Booleans with NURBS operands (one all-NURBS) ≤ 1.7e-15 |
+| P. Cut / Remove (Plasticity C · X) | `BodyCut`: `CutBody` sweeps the cut profile along the plane normal from −2·Reach to +2·Reach (`MeasureCutReach`) into a tool and splits the body with GeneralFuse into Inside = body ∩ tool and Outside = body − tool; an open chain is closed far outside the body on its left (`CloseCutChain`); sheets keep only their own faces (`FirstInside` / `FirstOutside`, no tool caps). `ProjectCutCurve` projects a SpaceCurve onto the cut plane. Feature steps `Cut` (11: Target, sketch `Profile` or one `Sections` SpaceCurve along `Plane.ZAxis`; the outside piece keeps the key, the inside piece is body `Step.Label` and becomes active; tool faces `Cut#N.Side(seg)`) and `Remove` (12: erases Target). `SurfaceIntersection` `FootReaches`: a NURBS–NURBS marching step only continues when the clamped foot really lies on both surfaces (≤ 10·precision), so branches end at a panel boundary | 🟢 BodyCutValidation K1–K7 · S1–S3: box / cylinder / spline / notch cuts rel ≤ 3.3e-13, keys and Remove bit-identical, refusals named; planar loft trim edge 2.3e-15, bonnet + character line along −z area kept rel 3.2e-7, bonnet + circle (holed sheet) rel 1.7e-6 (tessellation sag 5·10⁻⁶) · SolidArc W17 6/6 |
+| Q. Curve trim (Plasticity T) | `SketchTrim`: `IntersectProfileSegments` seeds crossings from polylines (24 samples per knot span / ≤ 45° arc piece) and refines them by Newton on the exact curves (lines, arcs, circles, B-splines; touching ends count). `TrimSketchCurve` removes the piece under the pick between neighbouring crossings: a line / arc is shortened or split (new curve, next identifier), a circle becomes the complementary arc, an uncrossed curve is erased whole, a crossed spline is refused 🚧 (no exact split in the point-defined forms). Constraints follow: length-type ones drop, direction / radius ones are copied to the new part, new ends are pinned `PointOnLine` / `PointOnCircle` to same-sketch cutters; `EraseSketchCurve` shifts curve references | 🟢 SketchTrimValidation R1–R7 28/28: crossings vs closed form ≤ 6.3e-16, line × spline count = sign changes, rectangle → 3 × 2 profile and circle → D (π/2) exact, solves move nothing, foreign cutters, whole-curve erase and refusals · SolidArc W18 6/6 (pentagram → star, area vs shoelace 1.1e-15) |
+| R. Editing (Plasticity G / R / S · Shift+D · J · O · P) | `BodyTransform`: `AffineMap` (ColumnX / Y / Z / Shift; `TranslationMap`, `RotationMap`, `ScalingMap`) moves every carrier exactly: a similarity maps planes, quadrics, tori and NURBS poles directly; a non-similar map (non-uniform scale) promotes conics and curved analytic faces to rational NURBS, and refuses rolling-ball and traced carriers with a reason 🚧; a singular map is refused; feature steps `Transform` (13: names carried unchanged), `Duplicate` (14: the body now, or as it stood after `Source`; faces `Label.Copy(name)`) and `Pipe` (15: radius `Size` along a SpaceCurve or a one-curve sketch; faces `Cap(Start / End)` and `Side(Path)`). `SketchEditing`: `OffsetSketchCurves` (lines and arcs exact, joints re-met, refusals for zero distance, vanishing pieces, inside-out loops), `JoinSketchModels` (welds ends within 10⁻⁶ in the base plane, drops duplicates), `PlaceSketchModel`, `SketchContactCondition`. `PathSweep` `PipeAlongCurve` sweeps a circle along any NURBS curve (rotation-minimising frames) | 🟢 SketchEditingValidation 8/8 (worst 2.2e-15) · BodyEditingValidation 9/9 (moved / turned / scaled volumes and names exact; pipe along a wave: 65 sections, deviation 1.3e-6 ≤ 10⁻⁴ · r) · SolidArc W19–W22 |
+| S. Sketch constraints UI (K) | `SketchConstraining`: SolveSpace's verbs on picked points / curves → solver constraints. `ProposeSketchConstraint` sorts the picks into points, lines, circles / arcs and splines and maps D (line → length, two points → distance, circle / arc → radius), N (two lines → signed angle), H / V (line, or two points level / plumb), O (coincident, point on line / circle, concentric), Q (equal length / radius), M (midpoint), Y (symmetric about a line), L (parallel, or tangent line–circle / circle–circle with internal tangency detected), [ (perpendicular), ] (lock where it is); wrong picks are refused by name ("Line1.Start already ends Line1"). `MeasureSketchConstraint` gives the current value (the D / N default), `NameSketchPick` / `DescribeSketchConstraint` the UI text. `DragSketchPoint` pins the dragged point with a temporary Fixed and lets the rest follow (minimum-norm Gauss–Newton); when the pin conflicts, it solves from the moved configuration, so the point lands as near the target as its constraints allow. **Splines (kinds 21–24):** O puts a point on the curve (normal offset to the nearest foot), H / V with an end point fixes the end direction, L with a curve meeting an end gives G1 (normalised tangent cross) and C gives G2 (tangency + κA − s·κB, circle κ = 1/r); a natural cubic spline refuses C (its end curvature is 0 by construction); exact dense gradients through the spline weights. **Reference dimensions:** `ProposeSketchReference` (Shift+D) makes a driven dimension: no equation, status Driven, Value = the measurement after the solve. **Links:** a point / circle linked to an earlier sketch is held (its unknowns frozen, so Fixed on it is redundant and drags refuse); regeneration re-projects it through world coordinates (`ProjectSketchLinks`, circle radii only between parallel planes) and notes dangling links on the step | 🟢 SketchConstrainingValidation S1–S10 118/118 (verb table 32 cases, measuring, rectangle DOF 4 → 2 → 1 → 0 with the redundant / conflicting partners named, drag ≤ 1e-9 (bead on a fixed rim lands at (2, 0)), exact strings, solved verbs ≤ 4.5e-15; S7 spline verbs 16 cases; S8 G1 in all 4 forms, G2 to a NURBS / arc (κ = 1/r, 1.1e-14) / line, DOF 6 → 5 → 4; S9 reference √13 → 5 with positions bit-equal; S10 links held bit-exact, Width 3 → 4 carries a later sketch's corner (3, 2) → (4, 2), XZ projection, dangling note) · SolidArc W23–W28 |
+| T. Incremental replay | `RegenerateFeatureTree(…, RegenerationCache*)`: after every step the replay state is saved as an immutable, shared checkpoint (a copy of the partition — slot tables and generations included — plus bodies, solved sketches, fitted curves, panels and Duplicate snapshots). `DigestFeatureStep` (`ReplayDigest`) writes every field a step reads, bit-exact, plus the current value of each parameter it binds; a SpaceCurve also carries the tree's Mirror planes, the only input read from later steps. The next regeneration restores the longest prefix whose digests match (rewinding to the source step of a newly requested Duplicate snapshot) and replays from the first changed step; digests are stored after the replay because capture rewrites signatures. A capturing run re-captures restored steps in place from the previous checkpoint and their resolutions (a signature depends only on the partition before the step and the resolved slot), so authoring never forces a replay just to capture | 🟢 ReplayValidation E1–E4: 138 randomized edits (parameter, literal, delete, truncate, restore) on the 9 catalogue trees and a 34-step studded plate, **0 differing bytes** vs a full replay on a fresh partition (step reports, tokens, names, sketches, curves, record stores, vertex positions, volume bits, active-body tessellation); resume points exact (10/10 trees); plate full replay 1.79 s → tail edit 0.40 s (4.5×), unchanged tree 0.44 ms, recording overhead within noise (−0.4 %); capture runs equal full capture replays including the written signatures (resumed 34/34) |
+| U. NURBS fillets / offsets (priority 10) | N1 `ParallelCarrier`: exact offset O = S + d·N of a NURBS surface (Weingarten derivatives, basis inversion, fold margin min(1 − dκᵢ)); SSI corrects onto both carriers. N2 rolling-ball fillets on NURBS supports: the spine is the SSI of two parallel carriers, chart breaks at every support knot, refused past the fold. N3 `CarrierApproximation` + `ApproximateBodyAsNurbs`: certified cubic B-spline stand-ins for rolling-ball / parallel faces and traced edges in their own chart (Greville interpolation, carrier C¹ breaks as double knots, position ≤ tolerance and normal ≤ angular tolerance on a 6 × 6 lattice per cell), tolerant edges / vertices of 2 × tolerance, refused atomically past the span cap. N4 face offsets and hollows of NURBS walls: the wall becomes a parallel carrier and its meetings with neighbouring carriers are exact traced intersections (`FaceChange` falls back to the SSI branch nearest the old edge when a carrier is procedural). N5 chamfers and variable fillets / chamfers on NURBS supports: the ball law runs on extended copies of the supports (`ExtendNurbsSurface`, 0.25 of the span past each end, so the end caps find their feet), a fold guard refuses any size past a support's curvature radius before assembly, open NURBS spines get a chamfer margin (clamped for periodic rims), and the chord carrier's peak curvature is the larger rail-turn rate (it used to be κ/(1 − r·κ) of the spine, infinite once the spine radius fell below r, which hung tessellation). Gates: `FreeformBlendValidation` P1–P4, F1–F3, C1–C2, O1–O3, A1–A4 |
+| V. Assemblies and drawings (priority 11) | A1 `JointSolver` (joint origins on analytic entities, the seven Fusion joint kinds with limits, the Joint feature step) and `AssemblyAnalysis` (mass with densities, interference). D1 `DrawingProjection`: orthographic views (six principal views and the isometric) with every non-seam edge, tangent edges flagged by the face normals, exact silhouettes (marching squares on the face chart for N·view = 0, every point polished onto the contour, trimmed by the chart winding number), hidden lines by exact rays toward the viewer through `IntersectCurveSurface` and `ClassifyFacePosition` (grazing hits discarded), each visibility change snapped to the exact outline crossing by a 2 × 2 Newton solve, and section views (`CutBodyAtPlane` on a scratch partition, cap edges as section outlines, even-odd hatching). D2 `DrawingSheet`: A4–A0 sheets laid out by first or third angle with exact shared view mappings, the largest standard scale that fits, automatic dimensions (overall sizes, hole positions, ⌀ / R leaders fitted from the strokes, tiered, collision-free), centre marks, the section cutting line, an ISO 7200-style title block with the ISO 5456-2 symbol; `DrawingExport` SVG and DXF R12. Gates: `AssemblyValidation` J1–J6, `DrawingValidation` DR1–DR15 |
+| W. Exchange (priority 4) | X1 `StlExchange`: `WriteStl` writes the watertight tessellation as binary STL (84 + 50 n bytes, little-endian, header never "solid…") or ASCII (9 significant digits, so both forms weld to the same corners); `ModelUnitMillimetres` scales metre models to millimetres. `ReadStl` detects the layout, welds on 32-bit coordinates and names every malformed input; `MeasureStlSoundness` counts open / non-manifold / misoriented sides, components, χ, divergence volume and area. X2 `StepExchange`: `WriteStep` writes solid bodies as STEP AP214 in millimetres — exact PLANE / CYLINDRICAL / CONICAL / SPHERICAL / TOROIDAL_SURFACE, LINE / CIRCLE / ELLIPSE and B-splines (rational where weighted) for NURBS carriers, certified cubic stand-ins (≤ 10⁻⁶) only for rolling-ball / parallel surfaces and traced curves; cavities as BREP_WITH_VOIDS; byte-stable. X3 `StepReading`: `ReadStep` / `ImportStepFile` read AP203 / AP214 / AP242 solids (MANIFOLD_SOLID_BREP, BREP_WITH_VOIDS) into `BodyBlueprint` → `AssembleBody` — analytic carriers, B-splines, surfaces of revolution / linear extrusion (converted to NURBS), OpenCascade seam and vertex-loop conventions, SI and inch units, tolerant edges where another kernel's geometry misses its own topology, whole-face loop reversals repaired; atomic (a refusal adds nothing). Evidence: `ExchangeValidation` EX1–EX13 (EX11 against 11 OpenCascade-authored fixtures in `Validation/StepFixtures`) and `Tooling/ExchangeCrossCheck.py` (trimesh for STL; OpenCascade for STEP export and for OCCT → kernel → OCCT import; `PrepareLinuxBuild.sh exchange` installs both). X4 `FeatureStepKind::Import` (18): one solid read from `Step.Exchange` (embedded STEP text) at `Step.ExchangeUnit` mm per model unit, faces named `Label.Face(k)` in file order, both fields in the replay digest; the SolidArc Import… / Export… use it (`SolidArcExchange`, W38, `ExchangeWalkthrough.txt`) |
+
+🚧 Step-5 plan-gate gaps (refused with a 🚧 reason, never built wrong): setback chamfers, mixed convexity beside a sharp edge, smooth / notch / partial overflow, and chamfers on traced or elliptical spines (ruled procedural carrier). Built since step 5: fillets on traced and elliptical spines on the exact procedural rolling-ball carrier (`RollingBallValidation` R1–R9), pinch and Várady–Rockwood setback vertex blends (`SetbackValidation` S1–S6), and cliff overflow, where a blend wider than its face consumes it and is trimmed by the face beyond (BlendValidation Overflow family). Caps on curved end faces and mitres between any two blend surfaces are built from exact or traced sections.
+
+🚧 Step-6 gaps (refused with a reason, never built wrong): self-intersection *removal* (clashes are detected and refused), joint extrusion of faces that share an edge, extrusion of curved faces, thickening of closed sheets and outward thickening, re-making blends across a changed face, and carriers beyond plane / cylinder / cone / sphere / torus.
+
+🚧 Step-7 gaps (refused with a reason, never built wrong): graph-constructive decomposition of sketches (§ M 🥈; today one numerical system), sketch-on-face (sketch planes are fixed placements), references into sketch geometry other than lines, circles and arcs, feature-semantic roles beyond sweeps (§ L 🥉). Incremental regeneration is built (row T): the replay resumes at the first changed step.
+
+🚧 Step-8 gaps (refused with a reason, never built wrong): pipes along paths other than lines and arcs, non-coaxial lofts (need a skinned surface), oblique sweeps, non-similar transforms of traced or contact edges and of rolling-ball faces (analytic carriers are promoted to NURBS since phase A1), marched sections that run out of points, analytic singular points beyond equal crossing cylinders, and face merges across closed loops (KEMR) on carriers other than planes.
+
+Next in the build order: step 9, `SolidArcWorkspace` (Vulkan + Slang). See `Documentation/PLAN-SolidArcArchitecture.md`.
