@@ -0,0 +1,239 @@
+# SolidArc assembly walkthrough — Alt+J (Joint; Fusion Assemble → Joint, Plasticity has none) places one body on
+# another by a joint origin on each: an edge offers its centre / midpoint, a face its centroid / axis. The card picks the
+# kind (R rigid · V revolute · S slider · C cylindrical · P pin-slot · L planar · B ball), F flips, drag fields stage a
+# preview, Enter applies one Joint step. Measure (I) on two bodies adds the interference verdict (clear with its gap,
+# contact, overlap with its volume drawn in red). A committed joint's values drag in the step card (staged preview,
+# one undo entry on release).
+# Run: SolidArcCapture --specimen --reset-files --recovery …/AssemblyRecovery.solidarc
+#      --document …/Assembly.solidarc --script Exhibits/SolidArc/Code/Scripts/AssemblyWalkthrough.txt
+# Bracket specimen Block1 (hole r 0.3 at (3, 1.25) through z 0 … 1); circles are pointed at 135° off +x, away from seams.
+
+# Placement snapped to the 0.1 grid, as these checks were written for (free placement is the default since ⑮ of Snapping).
+snap grid on
+
+# ① two more bodies: a pin Cylinder3 r 0.25 h 1.5 at (6, 1.25, 0) and a lever Block2 2 × 0.4 × 0.2 at (6, 4, 0)
+frames 3
+expect bodies == 1
+click @ConstructLauncher
+frames 2
+click @ConstructCylinder
+frames 2
+key Tab
+frames 2
+click @CombinationSeparate
+click @ConstructX
+key A Ctrl
+type 6
+click @ConstructY
+key A Ctrl
+type 1.25
+click @ConstructZ
+key A Ctrl
+type 0
+click @ConstructRadius
+key A Ctrl
+type 0.25
+click @ConstructHeight
+key A Ctrl
+type 1.5
+click @ConstructX
+frames 2
+click @ConstructCreate
+frames 3
+expect refused == 0
+click @ConstructLauncher
+frames 2
+click @ConstructBlock
+frames 2
+key Tab
+frames 2
+click @CombinationSeparate
+click @ConstructX
+key A Ctrl
+type 6
+click @ConstructY
+key A Ctrl
+type 4
+click @ConstructZ
+key A Ctrl
+type 0
+click @ConstructWidth
+key A Ctrl
+type 2
+click @ConstructDepth
+key A Ctrl
+type 0.4
+click @ConstructHeight
+key A Ctrl
+type 0.2
+click @ConstructX
+frames 2
+click @ConstructCreate
+frames 3
+expect refused == 0
+expect bodies == 3
+expect body-captions contains Cylinder3
+expect body-captions contains Block2
+expect centroid:Cylinder3 == (6.000000, 1.250000, 0.750000)
+key Space
+frames 3
+capture 179AssemblyParts
+
+# ② Alt+J opens the card in phase 0; the pin's top rim under the pointer offers its centre (triad: z blue out of the cap)
+key J Alt
+frames 2
+expect joint == 1
+expect joint-phase == 0
+expect joint-kind == Revolute
+move world 5.823223 1.426777 1.5
+frames 2
+expect joint-hover contains circle centre on Cylinder3
+capture 180JointHover
+
+# ③ click takes it as the moving origin; the hole's top rim on the bracket is the fixed one → phase 2 and a staged preview.
+#    Facing origins put the pin's cap on the hole's rim with the pin standing up out of it
+click world 5.823223 1.426777 1.5
+frames 2
+expect joint-phase == 1
+move world 2.787868 1.462132 1.0
+frames 2
+expect joint-hover contains circle centre on Block1
+click world 2.787868 1.462132 1.0
+frames 3
+expect joint-phase == 2
+expect joint-preview == 1
+expect joint-refusal == 0
+expect joint-picks contains circle centre on Cylinder3 -> circle centre on Block1
+expect preview-resumed > 0
+capture 181JointPreview
+
+# ④ F flips (origins aligned): the pin drops into the hole; Offset 0.25 (Ctrl+click types) lifts it 0.25 proud
+key F
+frames 2
+expect joint-flipped == 1
+click @JointOffset Left Ctrl
+key A Ctrl
+type 0.25
+key Enter
+frames 3
+expect joint-refusal == 0
+capture 182JointFlipped
+
+# ⑤ Enter applies one Joint step: the pin's centroid is (3, 1.25, 0.5) — on the hole axis, z −0.25 … 1.25
+key Enter
+frames 3
+expect joint == 0
+expect joint-commits == 1
+expect refused == 0
+expect joints == 1
+expect joint-gap ~ 0.25
+expect centroid:Cylinder3 == (3.000000, 1.250000, 0.500000)
+capture 183JointApplied
+
+# ⑥ the pin's rim (now in the hole) as the moving origin, then the pin's own cap: refused — the second origin must be on
+#    another body; Esc cancels
+key J Alt
+frames 2
+click world 2.823223 1.426777 1.25
