+key Escape
+frames 2
+key 4
+frames 1
+click world -0.95 0.0 2.0
+frames 2
+expect selected-bodies > 0
+key Escape
+frames 2
+
+# ⑪ a picked body is the cutter (KitOps cutter object): pick the separate insert body (0.4 × 0.4 × 0.14), Shift+K, it
+#    follows the pointer onto the cube's +x face, Ctrl turns its z onto the face normal (0.14 along x), a right-click
+#    places it, the pointer along the normal pulls it out, typed 0.03 sinks its centre 0.03 in: x 0.90 … 1.04 cuts
+#    0.10 × 0.4 × 0.4 = 0.016 out of the cube and the cutter is used up (0.0224): 7.525828330588459 − 0.0384
+key 4
+frames 1
+click world -0.5 -0.5 2.02
+frames 2
+expect selected-bodies == 1
+key K Shift
+frames 2
+expect knife == 1
+expect knife-mode == Object
+expect knife-placed == 0
