+
+# ⑭ every library cutter is drawn as the Construct primitives are: the press puts a base corner of the Triangle on the
+#    top face, the drag carries the opposite corner — the base runs corner to corner, x and y apart, 0.01 steps — and
+#    the release hands the pointer to the depth along the normal (typed 0.2 here); right-click cuts. The triangle
+#    filling a 0.4 × 0.4 base is half of it: 0.08 · 0.2 = 0.016. A Round hole typed 0.2 wide, clicked without a drag
+#    (the pointer would now carry its far corner), T straight through the 2 m cube: 0.01π · 2 = 0.0628318530718.
+click @SketchKnifeTool
