+# SolidArc surface-evaluation walkthrough (vehicle plan V8): zebra stripes and the deviation map on the synthetic
+# bonnet. Smooth data joins almost G1 by itself (8.5e-4 rad, gate C3) — invisible in any zebra — so ① lifts pole 2 of the
+# shared Section3 (mode 1 drag, ≈ 20 mm): front (Section1–3) and rear (Section3–6) lofts joined G0 then crease along
+# Section3 and the stripes kink. ② The rear loft redone G2: the stripes run smoothly across. ③ The deviation map: a needle
+# from every imported limit point (286, including 5 check loops never lofted) to its foot on the panels, coloured on
+# 0 … 0.2 mm — the lifted pole shows as red needles (the edit leaves the scan). ④ A fresh bonnet lofted through all six
+# sections, Alt+X: the stripes continue across the mirror seam at x = 0 (look-ahead tangents).
+# Run: SolidArcCapture --specimen --reset-files --recovery …/EvaluationRecovery.solidarc
+#      --document …/Evaluation.solidarc --script Scripts/SurfaceEvaluationWalkthrough.txt
+# Click points lie on the analytic bonnet at ξ = 0.5 (x = 0.375); the dragged pole is pole 2 of Section3 at
+# (0.50298, 0.41799, 0.81056), as in VehicleSurfacingWalkthrough.txt.
+
+# Placement snapped to the 0.1 grid, as these checks were written for (free placement is the default since ⑮ of Snapping).
+snap grid on
+
+# ① bonnet: lift pole 2 of Section3, front loft, rear loft G0
