+# SolidArc trim / split walkthrough — Plasticity C (command:cut) splits a body by the focused sketch or the
+# selected curve (curves are seen along the view axis); the inside piece comes out picked in mode 4, so X deletes it.
+# Vehicle flow from the BMW study: loft a panel → C with a character line → X the unwanted piece.
+# T (command:trim) removes the piece of a sketch curve under the pointer between its crossings (hover previews it in red).
+# Run: SolidArcCapture --specimen --reset-files --recovery …/TrimSplitRecovery.solidarc
+#      --document …/TrimSplit.solidarc --script Exhibits/SolidArc/Code/Scripts/TrimSplitWalkthrough.txt
+# Closed forms: box 2 × 1 × 1 cut at x = 0.6 (line drawn upward: inside = left = x < 0.6) → 0.6 + 1.4; core r 0.3 → 0.09π;
+# pentagram A(1,0) → C(1.6,1.9) → E(0,0.7) → B(2,0.7) → D(0.4,1.9) trimmed to its star: shoelace area 1.237928331467.
+
+# Placement snapped to the 0.1 grid, as these checks were written for (free placement is the default since ⑮ of Snapping).
+snap grid on
+
+# ① empty document, Top view: a 2 × 1 rectangle extruded 1 (New)
+key N Ctrl
+frames 2
+expect steps == 0
+key Keypad7
+frames 2
+key Q Shift
+frames 2
+click world 0.0 0.0 0.0
+frames 2
+click world 2.0 1.0 0.0
+frames 2
+key F
+frames 2
+key E
+frames 2
+click @BevelSize
+key A Ctrl
+type 1
+key Enter
+frames 2
+key Enter
+frames 2
+expect steps == 2
+expect volume ~ 2
+expect bodies == 1
+
+# ② C with nothing to cut with explains what it needs
+key Escape
+frames 2
+key C
+frames 2
+expect status contains focus a sketch step or select a curve
+expect steps == 2
+
+# ②b Ctrl+Alt+click an edge picks its ring (Blender): the top front edge along x walks front → bottom → back → top
+#    faces, so the four edges along x come picked. Alt+click is Blender's edge loop: a box corner has three edges (a
+#    pole), so the loop is that edge alone. Alt+A lets them go
+key 2
+frames 2
+move world 1.0 0.0 1.0
+frames 2
+click world 1.0 0.0 1.0 Left Ctrl Alt
+frames 2
+expect selected-edges == 4
+expect ring-picks == 1
+capture 294EdgeRing
+click world 1.0 0.0 1.0 Left Alt
+frames 2
+expect selected-edges == 1
+expect ring-picks == 2
+key A Alt
+frames 2
+expect selected-edges == 0
+
+# ③ Shift+A line across the box at x = 0.6 (drawn upward), Enter finishes the open chain, C splits the box in two
+key A Shift
+frames 2
+click world 0.6 -0.5 0.0
+frames 2
+click world 0.6 1.5 0.0
+frames 2
+key Enter
+frames 2
+expect focused-caption == Line1
+key C
+frames 3
+expect refused == 0
